================================================================================
WHAT THIS FILE ESTABLISHES
================================================================================

  One arm of the DISCRIMINATING pair of the controlled A/B the AAP mandates
  (0.5.1, 0.9.1): the pinned tainted-sql-string rule from the pinned Opengrep
  ruleset, run over Spark's own in-scope Scala file
  sql/hive/src/main/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/hive/client/HiveShim.scala,
  with taint analysis as the SOLE analysis difference between the two arms. It
  carries this arm's exact command, its argv delta against its sibling, the
  scan root and the pinned HEAD it ran against, the engine, rule and ruleset
  identities it ran under, its exit code, its wall time, the findings it
  produced with every line and every dataflow trace step, and the output's
  byte size and sha256 measured from the file on disk after the write.

  An A/B proves a capability only through the CONTRAST between two invocations
  that differ in one setting. Enabled-in-config is not proof (AAP 0.1.3), so
  this file reports the contrast as it came out and states the verdict for the
  PAIR as well as the result for this arm. The pair's verdict is below, and it
  is the run's answer to whether Opengrep's taint engine is active on Spark's
  own Scala.

================================================================================
WHY THIS FILE IS UNDER logs/ AND NEVER UNDER raw/
================================================================================

  Two independent reasons, either sufficient (AAP 0.5.1, 0.6.1). First, raw/
  is RUNNER-ONLY: it receives exactly one artifact per tool that writes one
  and nothing else, ever, so an A/B SARIF landing there would overwrite the
  opengrep.sarif the Stage 3 runner writes and the dataset would then be built
  from an A/B over ONE file instead of a scan over the whole scope. Second,
  this is one of the run's two deliberate second appearances: Opengrep appears
  here as the taint A/B subject and again as one of the nine scanned runners;
  Joern appears as a runner and again as the capability probe's subject. Each
  second appearance writes outside raw/ and contributes NO dataset row (AAP
  0.3.2).

